      "content": "While the primary mechanism is biological, the perceived \"flow\" is an experienced psychological effect of achieving physiological coherence. When your breathing becomes rhythmic and controlled, it synchronizes your heart rate variability with your breath cycle. This resonance can create a profound sense of internal stillness or energy, which practitioners often describe as a tangible feeling. Therefore, it is both a measurable biological state and a deeply felt holistic experience.",
      "source": "target",
